<title>UK: LME copper eases in late inter-office trade.</title>
<headline>LME copper eases in late inter-office trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper prices eased slightly in late inter-office trading on Thursday, after thrashing around in ring trading.</p>
<p>By 1900 GMT three month copper was at $2,332/2,335, compared with a kerb close of $2,339, but well off a low of $2,312.</p>
<p>Aluminium eased a touch to $1,655/1,658 by 1900 GMT from a kerb close of $1,658.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
